\f0\fs24 \cf0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::2>
\f1\b\fs36 Core conception\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f2 The elliptical-rail apparatus is a Shakti Engineering design developed for Project Kebab from Johnny Stoat\'92s vague requirements and the accumulated test data from earlier, less stable apparatuses.\
Johnny claims intellectual ownership and presents the machine as evidence of his engineering genius. He did not design it.\
The design thinking belongs to the Shakti engineering team working off-page. Johnny contributes ambition, requirements, interference, escalating demands and a willingness to test things that more competent people would prefer to model first.\
The testing scenes should expose the gap between Johnny\'92s claims and his actual understanding. He knows enough vocabulary to talk about rotational speed, phase, spatial geometry, coherence and related parameters. He can demand changes and interpret favourable results as proof of his genius. Once discussion reaches why the apparatus behaves as it does, or how the engineering team has made multiple motions interact coherently, Johnny is out of his depth.\
The apparatus is sophisticated because Eloise\'92s engineers are very good at solving difficult problems.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::2>
\f1\b\fs36 Apparatus chamber and approach\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f2 The apparatus occupies the established Project Kebab chamber in the deepest, most isolated part of the Ruined Castle weapons-development complex.\
The final approach should make that isolation physical.\
A long secure passage connects the chamber access zone to the rest of the Kebab sector. It is broad enough and high enough to drive a full-size truck through, because the chamber must accept heavy components, maintenance equipment and replacement machinery. The passage also supplies deliberate empty distance between the apparatus and occupied parts of the installation. It should feel engineered as a safety gap rather than merely oversized circulation.\
Routine personnel transit along this final approach can use Shakti 
\f1\b \strokec2 service runabouts
\f2\b0 \strokec2 : compact electric personnel carriers resembling industrial utility carts rather than recreational golf carts. Two such vehicles can carry Johnny, Sarah, Chip, the Sages and accompanying engineering staff to the chamber without making the journey feel absurdly pedestrian.\
The apparatus chamber itself is a buried machine hall several storeys high. It must be large enough for the elliptical apparatus to move as a whole, not merely for carriages to travel around the ellipse.\
The chamber therefore includes:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 a broad clear floor around the machine;\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 enough circulation for heavy maintenance vehicles and lifting equipment;\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 fixed perimeter galleries on the chamber walls;\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 stair towers or lifts reaching multiple elevations;\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 high inspection positions from which a person can look down across the whole ellipse;\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 retractable, hinged or removable maintenance bridges that can reach the parked apparatus and then clear its moving envelope;\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 sufficient overhead and lateral clearance for the complete rail-and-cradle structure to slew and tilt.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 Johnny, Sarah, Chip and the Sages can therefore walk around the parked apparatus, inspect it at floor level and gain elevation over it during an unveiling or commissioning sequence.\
This does not replace the established remote Project Kebab control room. The control room remains significantly removed from the apparatus chamber and has no direct observation window. The chamber\'92s galleries and maintenance access exist for physical inspection, servicing and commissioning, not as the normal place from which hazardous live tests are operated.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::2>
\f1\b\fs36 Primary structure\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f2 The apparatus is built around a large elliptical rail carrying independently moving disc assemblies.\
The ellipse is not fixed to the chamber floor. The complete rail is carried in a massive steerable cradle broadly analogous to the mounting of a large radio telescope.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 \strokec2 Azimuth system:
\f2\b0 \strokec2  the cradle sits on a large, precisely levelled circular steel ring track built into the chamber floor. Multiple powered wheel bogies or trucks support the mass and drive the entire structure around the ring, rotating the ellipse horizontally about a vertical axis.\

\f1\b \strokec2 Elevation system:
\f2\b0 \strokec2  the rail-and-cradle assembly pivots about a transverse elevation axis carried by massive side structures. Large semicircular bull gears, geared sectors or an equivalent heavy geared mechanism are attached to the rotating structure. Motor-driven pinions and gearboxes act on them to raise or lower the plane of the ellipse.\

\f1\b \strokec2 Counterweights:
\f2\b0 \strokec2  large steel, composite or concrete counterweights balance the rail, carriage assemblies and supporting structure about the elevation axis. The intention is not to make the apparatus light. It is to keep its centre of mass close enough to the pivot that the elevation drives are controlling a balanced structure rather than attempting to lift the machine bodily every time its orientation changes.\
The global mounting therefore gives the entire apparatus two additional controlled variables:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 azimuth;\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 elevation.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 These are deliberately slow, massive motions. They contrast with the much faster local motions of the carriages, articulated arms, epicycles and spinning Gyges discs.\
Each assembly begins with a carriage travelling around the rail.\
Mounted to each carriage is a primary articulated extensible arm. The arm can:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 extend and retract;\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 incline towards or away from the centre;\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 vary the effective orbital radius of its disc;\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 raise or lower the disc relative to the other discs.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 At the end of the primary arm is another articulation supporting a secondary arm.\
The secondary arm can rotate around the end of the primary arm, giving each disc an additional independent circular motion: effectively an epicycle whose centre is itself travelling around the larger elliptical system.\
At the end of the secondary arm sits the final articulated disc harness.\
The exact articulation axes, gimbal ranges, drive systems, bearings, propulsion and control architecture remain unspecified unless a mechanical detail produces comedy, character conflict or necessary plot information.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::2>
\f1\b\fs36 Disc excitation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f2 Project Kebab does not rotate a Gyges disc like a record on a turntable.\
The final harness spins the disc end-over-end, as though it were a coin being continuously tossed without ever being released.\
The spin axis passes approximately through a diameter of the disc rather than perpendicular to its faces.\
The faces therefore repeatedly change orientation as the disc flips through successive rotations.\
Each disc can participate simultaneously in several kinds of motion:\
Main orbit \'97 its carriage moves around the elliptical rail.\
Primary displacement \'97 the extensible arm changes radius, height and inclination.\
Local orbit \'97 the secondary arm carries the disc around an epicycle whose centre is itself moving.\
Harness orientation \'97 the final articulation changes the attitude of the disc.\
Disc excitation \'97 the disc spins end-over-end like a perpetually tossed coin.\
Global azimuth \'97 the complete elliptical apparatus rotates horizontally on its mounting ring.\
Global elevation \'97 the complete elliptical apparatus tilts about its elevation axis.\
In operation the apparatus can resemble a mechanised model of a demented solar system: planets moving on eccentric paths while describing epicycles, changing orbital radius, climbing above and below each other and flipping continuously.\
The global cradle makes the visual conception more extreme without changing its logic: the entire mechanised solar system can itself slew and tilt.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::2>
\f1\b\fs36 Geometry and motion are the machine\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f2 The apparatus is not best understood as a conventional machine containing several Gyges discs.\
The geometry and motion are the machine.\
The hardware exists to control relationships between excited Gyges fields.\
Experimental variables can include:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 individual disc rotational speed;\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 relative rotational phase;\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 carriage position;\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 orbital velocity;\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 arm extension;\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 relative height;\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 inclination;\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 epicyclic speed;\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 epicyclic phase;\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 harness attitude;\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 separation;\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 relative angular relationships;\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 overall spatial geometry;\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 apparatus azimuth;\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 apparatus elevation;\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 coherence between two or more fields;\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 and related parameters discovered through testing.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 Project Kebab dialogue can range through disc rotational speed, relative phase, spatial geometry, coherence and the like without requiring the narrator to explain every variable.\
Individual discs become substantially more consequential when their fields enter suitable relationships and begin behaving as one coherent system.\
The apparatus\'92s particular danger lies not merely in its ability to place the discs in unusual configurations, but in its ability to drive them rapidly through changing configurations while maintaining coherence.\
The steerable cradle extends that principle one level outward. The machine can alter not only the geometry of the discs relative to one another, but the orientation of the entire interacting system relative to the surrounding world.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::2>
\f1\b\fs36 The rail plane\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f2 The plane of the elliptical track is no longer fixed in canon.\
The rail sits in a steerable cradle with controlled azimuth and elevation. Its orientation is therefore an experimental variable rather than a permanent architectural condition.\
The apparatus can rotate horizontally on its floor ring and tilt about its elevation axis while the carriage-and-arm systems retain their own independent motion.\
The exact parked or home orientation remains open, as do the maximum azimuth and elevation ranges.\
Changing the apparatus orientation may alter its relationship to:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 gravity;\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 planetary orientation;\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 magnetic or other environmental fields;\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 a multi-universal reference condition discovered empirically during testing.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 The apparatus need not acquire this ability because Johnny requests it.\
Shakti Engineering may add it because the accumulated data indicate apparatus orientation matters.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::2>
\f1\b\fs36 Rubber Geometry\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f2 The pentagram objective does not require five discs to occupy a neat schoolbook star.\
In rubber-sheet geometry, forms can be stretched and continuously deformed while retaining their relevant topological relationships.\
Project Kebab can exploit that idea directly.\
The pentagram need not be rigid.\
Five discs can preserve the underlying five-point relationship while:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 distances vary;\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 angles change;\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 vertices rise and fall;\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 the structure stretches;\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 it compresses;\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 it skews;\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 individual vertices describe epicycles;\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 the arrangement becomes non-planar.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 The experimentally interesting object is therefore not one perfect pentagram.\
It is the family of continuously deforming pentagrams.\
The machine can move among members of that family while phase, distance, height, inclination and coherence change continuously.\
\'93Rubber Geometry\'94 also provides comic territory:\
\'93Rubber Geometry.\'94\
\'93It\'92s got nothing to do with the dimensions of your condoms.\'94\
\'93Or your\'97\'94\
\'93Johnny.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::2>
\f1\b\fs36 The concealed objective\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f2 At the point of Testing the elliptical-rail apparatus, Johnny is publicly testing it as a two-disc machine.\
He is concealing the five-disc pentagram objective.\
Sarah has obtained enough evidence from Rotherhithe to oppose increasing the number of Gyges discs.\
Johnny appears to comply.\
Shakti Engineering therefore delivers an improved two-disc apparatus.\
What is not advertised is that the architecture is modular.\
Additional carriage-and-arm assemblies can be mounted on the same rail.\
Johnny already has two discs and needs three more to satisfy the Sages\'92 objective.\
The two-disc test should establish the legitimate engineering virtues of the apparatus while its scalability remains hiding in plain sight.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::2>
\f1\b\fs36 What the two-disc test can demonstrate\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f2 Without revealing the pentagram objective, the apparatus can demonstrate:\
